            mark = "this is a case of a phrase where we don't hear the speaker use a ""low"" pitch target. instead, they seem to be purposefully ending at a mid level. using an estimated min value of 135 leads to a ""3"" on the Levels tier here, which accords with our intuitions. 135 itself is not meaningful, and so a labeller with the same intuition may end up putting ""150"" or ""120"" here, for example." 
